; Regression: `*r` on a NON-OPTIONAL `ref[T]` is a hard error (2026-08-27).
;
; The fifth gate on a borrowed reference, and the one the other four were
; building towards. A `ref[T]` reads and writes as its pointee, so `*` on one
; is the POINTER idiom applied to a value that is not a pointer -- the same
; line report_ref_arithmetic# draws for `+`.
;
; It could only land after the transparent readings existed AND the tree was
; swept: until then `*r` was the only spelling that worked.
;
; The nullable `ref[T]?` is deliberately NOT judged -- it is Option[ref[T]],
; no transparent reading exists for an Option, and `*opt` stays the spelling.
; See deref_of_optional_ref_ok.scaly for that half.
;
; xfail: dereferencing a reference

function reads(r: ref[int]) returns int
    *r

var a: int 7
Console.println "unreachable"
